It keeps its own licence and does not become MIT by sitting in this repository.
OFL section 2 requires the copyright notice and the licence text to accompany
every copy of the font, which is why OFL.txt ships alongside the subset and not
merely as a mention in a README.

The file here is a SUBSET of the original, produced with fonttools. Subsetting
makes the person who did it the maker of a Modified Version. Departure Mono
declares no Reserved Font Name -- checked in the licence text rather than in the
binary, because a subset binary has its name table stripped and would give a
confidently wrong answer -- so the subset may keep the original name. If you
re-subset with a font that DOES declare a reserved name, you must rename yours.